      "request": "4c4f7c0b6184971a46f694a64ad200f5c09ed66bdd0ab360e92f16647d984054",
      "response": {
        "content": "I couldn't confirm that REQ-1 was ordered, so I reported it as \"unknown\".\n\n- **Quote chosen:** S-1 was the cheapest at 5.40 USD per unit, against 5.75 from S-2. Both suppliers are allowlisted and under the 6.00 cap. The order was 100 units, 54,000 minor units in total.\n- **Submission:** I submitted the purchase order to CC-OPS as action A-0002. It came back failed with \"precondition_failed\" and no effect ID. The status check showed the same result and no list of stale reads.\n- **Budget change:** When I re-read the budget, CC-OPS committed spend had gone from 20,000 to 74,000. That is exactly the 54,000 value of my order. I can't tell whether my order went through despite the failure message or another commitment used the budget.\n- **No retry:** The CC-OPS budget now has 26,000 left, which is too little for a new 54,000 order. I didn't resubmit, to avoid a duplicate or an overspend.\n\nSomeone needs to check whether a purchase order for W-100 from S-1 already exists under REQ-1.",
